at":"2026-08-03"},{"id":"hedera-volume","title":"DefiLlama Hedera DEX volume API","publisher":"DefiLlama","url":"https://api.llama.fi/overview/dexs/Hedera?dataType=dailyVolume","source_role":"independent-data","checked_at":"2026-08-03"},{"id":"hedera-stables","title":"DefiLlama stablecoin supply by chain API","publisher":"DefiLlama","url":"https://stablecoins.llama.fi/stablecoinchains","source_role":"independent-data","checked_at":"2026-08-03"}],"forensic_analysis":{"version":"forensic-analysis-v1","observation_snapshot":{"observed_at":"2026-08-03T17:23:37.879Z","observation_completed_at":"2026-08-03T17:23:58.550Z","provider":"DefiLlama","method":"One sequential client run: stablecoinchains once, then the latest historicalChainTvl point and provider-reported 24-hour and 30-day fee, revenue, and DEX aggregates for each chain. Currency aggregates were rounded to cents. Same-day historical points can be revised after this retrieval window.","historical_tvl_point_date":"2026-08-03","latest_tvl_usd":24658328,"peak_tvl_usd":213960353,"peak_tvl_date":"2025-01-18","tvl_drawdown_pct":88.48,"stablecoin_supply":{"pegged_usd":36603338.6957305,"pegged_aud":836.7952098107663,"pegged_chf":81557.43684850691,"pegged_sgd":38990.60908060501},"dex_volume_24h_usd":618102,"dex_volume_30d_usd":72889336,"fees_24h_usd":2618.24,"fees_30d_usd":239074.77,"revenue_24h_usd":336.24,"revenue_30d_usd":43750.51},"outcome":{"label":"middling","summary":"Hedera is a functioning enterprise-oriented network with a middling economic outcome. In the DefiLlama snapshot begun at 2026-08-03T17:23:37.879Z, the latest 2026-08-03 point was $24.7 million TVL, 88.5% below the January 2025 peak, alongside $36.6 million of dollar stablecoins, $72.9 million of 30-day DEX volume, $239,075 of fees, and $43,751 of retained revenue. Its identifiable Council and native services provide an accountable operating model, but current consensus admission remains permissioned and the independent capital and revenue observations do not validate broad enterprise adoption. These figures are a point-in-time snapshot.","confidence":"high","as_of":"2026-08-03","source_refs":["hedera-tvl","hedera-stables","hedera-volume","hedera-fees","hedera-revenue","hedera-faq"]},"why":{"summary":"Observed: Hedera retains modest stablecoin, DEX, fee, and revenue activity, while TVL remains almost ninety percent below peak. Documented design: the network chose hashgraph consensus, predictable service pricing, native token and consensus services, EVM compatibility, and governance by a rotating council of named organizations. It later moved the open-source codebase into Linux Foundation Decentralized Trust, but its own FAQ still describes live consensus nodes as permissioned. Strategic inference: identifiable operators and specialized services can lower procurement and operational friction for enterprise workloads, while the same admission model narrows permissionless credibility and does not automatically create composable liquidity. The 2023 precompile exploit and the decision to disable proxies demonstrate fast coordinated response and concentrated intervention power at the same time. Neither operator transaction claims nor Council membership is treated here as independent proof of durable fee-paying demand.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["hedera-journey","hedera-governance","hedera-hiero","hedera-faq","hedera-incident","hedera-incident-independent","hedera-tvl","hedera-fees","hedera-revenue"]},"strategic_choices":[{"decision":"Govern the network through a term-limited council of identifiable global organizations.","consequence":"Members provide accountability and operational coordination, but governance and consensus admission remain concentrated relative to permissionless validator systems.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["hedera-governance","hedera-faq"]},{"decision":"Offer native consensus and token services alongside EVM smart contracts.","consequence":"Some enterprise workloads can avoid contract overhead, while developers and auditors must reason about interactions between native services, precompiles, and EVM applications.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["hedera-journey","hedera-incident"]},{"decision":"Donate the core codebase to Linux Foundation Decentralized Trust as Project Hiero.","consequence":"Development governance becomes more open and vendor-neutral, but code governance alone does not make live consensus-node admission permissionless.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["hedera-hiero","hedera-faq"]},{"decision":"Use coordinated network controls during the 2023 precompile exploit.","consequence":"Operators contained further access while patching the defect, showing response capacity and the practical power of a small known operator set.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["hedera-incident","hedera-incident-independent"]}],"counterfactual":{"summary":"Opening consensus-node admission earlier could have improved neutrality and reduced the gap between open-source branding and live participation, but it would have weakened the Council''s direct control over operator quality and incident coordination. Building only EVM contracts on an existing chain would have avoided a new consensus and governance system, but also surrendered native ordered-consensus and token-service differentiation. The reviewed evidence does not show that either alternative would have produced more enterprise revenue or prevented the precompile defect.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["hedera-governance","hedera-hiero","hedera-faq","hedera-incident","hedera-fees","hedera-revenue"]},"watch":[{"signal":"Permissionless-node milestones and the actual composition of consensus operators.","implication":"Open admission with diversified stake would reduce the principal governance objection; repeated roadmap deferral would make the permissioned model a durable feature rather than a transition.","source_refs":["hedera-governance","hedera-faq"]},{"signal":"TVL, stablecoins, DEX volume, fees, and retained revenue tracked separately from raw transaction counts.","implication":"Growth in independent economic measures would support durable demand; high operator-reported throughput without revenue would not.","source_refs":["hedera-tvl","hedera-stables","hedera-volume","hedera-fees","hedera-revenue"]},{"signal":"Security incidents at the boundary between native services, precompiles, and EVM applications.","implication":"A quiet operating record and broader audit coverage would support the hybrid-service design; another boundary failure would increase integration-risk weight.","source_refs":["hedera-incident","hedera-incident-independent"]}],"unknowns":[{"question":"When, under what admission rules, and with what stake distribution will non-Council consensus nodes be allowed?","resolution_trigger":"A deployed permissionless-node release with an auditable operator set."},{"question":"How concentrated is fee-paying demand by application or enterprise customer?","resolution_trigger":"An independent entity-level fee and transaction decomposition."},{"question":"What portion of current activity is subsidized by ecosystem grants or treasury allocations?","resolution_trigger":"Reconciled grant flows matched to application-level usage and fees."},{"question":"How much undistributed or restricted HBAR is controlled by Council-linked or ecosystem entities?","resolution_trigger":"A current audited treasury and restriction schedule."}],"review":{"status":"current","last_reviewed_at":"2026-08-03","next_review_at":"2026-08-10","reviewer":"chaindump-research-desk"}}}')
)
UPDATE chain_facts AS facts
SET
  data = CASE facts.dimension
    WHEN 'synthesis' THEN json_set(
      facts.data,
      '$.forensic_analysis',
      json(json_extract((SELECT payload FROM causal_seed), '$.forensic_analysis'))
    )
    WHEN '_meta' THEN json_set(
      facts.data,
      '$.forensic_analysis_version', 'forensic-analysis-v1',
      '$.last_reviewed', '2026-08-03',
      '$.next_review_at',
      json_extract(
        (SELECT payload FROM causal_seed),
        '$.forensic_analysis.review.next_review_at'
      )
    )
    ELSE facts.data
  END
  ,
  sources = CASE
    WHEN facts.dimension = 'synthesis' THEN (
      SELECT json_group_array(json(source_json))
      FROM (
        SELECT source_json
        FROM (
          SELECT
            CASE
              WHEN new_source.value IS NULL THEN old_source.value
              ELSE json_set(
                json_patch(old_source.value, new_source.value),
                '$.checked_at',
                CASE
                  WHEN json_extract(old_source.value, '$.checked_at')
                    > json_extract(new_source.value, '$.checked_at')
                    THEN json_extract(old_source.value, '$.checked_at')
                  ELSE COALESCE(
                    json_extract(new_source.value, '$.checked_at'),
                    json_extract(old_source.value, '$.checked_at')
                  )
                END
              )
            END AS source_json,
            old_source.key AS position
          FROM json_each(COALESCE(facts.sources, '[]')) AS old_source
          LEFT JOIN json_each(
            json_extract((SELECT payload FROM causal_seed), '$.sources')
          ) AS new_source
            ON json_extract(new_source.value, '$.url')
              = json_extract(old_source.value, '$.url')
          WHERE json_extract(old_source.value, '$.url') IS NULL
            OR old_source.key = (
              SELECT MIN(candidate.key)
              FROM json_each(COALESCE(facts.sources, '[]')) AS candidate
              WHERE json_extract(candidate.value, '$.url')
                = json_extract(old_source.value, '$.url')
            )
          UNION ALL
          SELECT new_source.value AS source_json, 10000 + new_source.key AS position
          FROM json_each(
            json_extract((SELECT payload FROM causal_seed), '$.sources')
          ) AS new_source
          WHERE NOT EXISTS (
            SELECT 1
            FROM json_each(COALESCE(facts.sources, '[]')) AS existing
            WHERE json_extract(existing.value, '$.url')
              = json_extract(new_source.value, '$.url')
          )
        )
        ORDER BY position
      )
    )
    ELSE facts.sources
  END
  ,
  updated_at = '2026-08-03'
WHERE facts.chain = json_extract((SELECT payload FROM causal_seed), '$.chain')
  AND facts.dimension IN ('synthesis', '_meta');
-- canonical-case-end Hedera

