endent-data","checked_at":"2026-08-03"},{"id":"gnosis-fees","title":"DefiLlama Gnosis fees API","publisher":"DefiLlama","url":"https://api.llama.fi/overview/fees/Gnosis?dataType=dailyFees","source_role":"independent-data","checked_at":"2026-08-03"},{"id":"gnosis-revenue","title":"DefiLlama Gnosis revenue API","publisher":"DefiLlama","url":"https://api.llama.fi/overview/fees/Gnosis?dataType=dailyRevenue","source_role":"independent-data","checked_at":"2026-08-03"},{"id":"gnosis-volume","title":"DefiLlama Gnosis DEX volume API","publisher":"DefiLlama","url":"https://api.llama.fi/overview/dexs/Gnosis?dataType=dailyVolume","source_role":"independent-data","checked_at":"2026-08-03"},{"id":"gnosis-stables","title":"DefiLlama stablecoin supply by chain API","publisher":"DefiLlama","url":"https://stablecoins.llama.fi/stablecoinchains","source_role":"independent-data","checked_at":"2026-08-03"}],"forensic_analysis":{"version":"forensic-analysis-v1","observation_snapshot":{"observed_at":"2026-08-03T17:23:37.879Z","observation_completed_at":"2026-08-03T17:23:58.550Z","provider":"DefiLlama","method":"One sequential client run: stablecoinchains once, then the latest historicalChainTvl point and provider-reported 24-hour and 30-day fee, revenue, and DEX aggregates for each chain. Currency aggregates were rounded to cents. Same-day historical points can be revised after this retrieval window.","historical_tvl_point_date":"2026-08-03","latest_tvl_usd":96599659,"peak_tvl_usd":291424311,"peak_tvl_date":"2024-12-17","tvl_drawdown_pct":66.85,"stablecoin_supply":{"pegged_usd":16354721.916508343,"pegged_var":1639.0877284640503,"pegged_eur":22035029.214089204,"pegged_chf":1857327.654309606,"pegged_gbp":1996.5761604046531,"pegged_real":479949.5531885662,"pegged_ars":5977.751640701662,"pegged_clp":5062.01596694746,"pegged_cop":6052.298446999369,"pegged_mxn":4119.705888712125,"pegged_pen":1393.3516345207584},"dex_volume_24h_usd":3318551.2,"dex_volume_30d_usd":150103176.08,"fees_24h_usd":9040.87,"fees_30d_usd":436345.75,"revenue_24h_usd":455.2,"revenue_30d_usd":24099.35},"outcome":{"label":"successful","summary":"Gnosis is a successful specialist chain for inexpensive, stable-value EVM settlement, although it is not a leading general-purpose liquidity venue. In the DefiLlama snapshot begun at 2026-08-03T17:23:37.879Z, the latest 2026-08-03 point was $96.6 million TVL, 66.9% below the December 2024 peak, with $150.1 million of 30-day DEX volume, $436,346 of fees, and $24,099 of retained revenue. Its multi-currency stablecoin supply and continuing activity support a durable niche, while the June 2026 Gnosis Pay module exploit and precautionary canonical-bridge pause expose application and bridge-governance dependencies. These figures are a point-in-time snapshot.","confidence":"high","as_of":"2026-08-03","source_refs":["gnosis-tvl","gnosis-stables","gnosis-volume","gnosis-fees","gnosis-revenue","gnosis-pay-incident","gnosis-pay-independent"]},"why":{"summary":"Observed: Gnosis retains more capital and DEX activity than many specialist chains, but TVL is below peak and protocol revenue remains modest. Documented design: xDai made stable-value gas a first-class user experience; the Gnosis merger aligned the chain with GNO staking; the 2022 Merge replaced a small authority set with Ethereum-derived proof of stake; and bridge governors retained explicit cross-chain controls. The chain later used an encrypted mempool as a live neutrality experiment. Strategic inference: compatibility with Ethereum clients, cheap stable gas, a large validator set, and payment-oriented products created a durable settlement niche without requiring Gnosis to win the base-asset or rollup race. The trade-off is layered trust: validators, bridge governors, stablecoin issuers, application modules, and Shutter keypers secure different boundaries. The 2026 card-safe exploit was not a consensus failure, but the bridge pause shows how an application incident can activate chain-adjacent control.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["gnosis-about","gnosis-merge","gnosis-merge-independent","gnosis-bridge","gnosis-bridge-decisions","gnosis-shutter","gnosis-pay-incident","gnosis-pay-independent","gnosis-tvl","gnosis-volume","gnosis-revenue"]},"strategic_choices":[{"decision":"Keep xDai as the native gas asset while using GNO for proof-of-stake security.","consequence":"Users receive predictable stable-value gas and stakers retain a separate security asset, but value capture and issuer dependencies are split across tokens.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["gnosis-about","gnosis-merge"]},{"decision":"Merge xDai and Gnosis governance, then replace the authority model with Ethereum-style proof of stake.","consequence":"The chain gained a much larger validator set and shared client architecture while accepting the operational complexity of a full beacon chain.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["gnosis-merge","gnosis-merge-independent"]},{"decision":"Govern canonical bridges through named governors and validators while adding light-client and multi-oracle paths.","consequence":"The network can pause and harden cross-chain flows, but bridge security and emergency power remain distinct from base consensus.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["gnosis-bridge","gnosis-bridge-decisions"]},{"decision":"Deploy threshold-encrypted transaction submission through Shutter.","consequence":"Users can reduce public-mempool front-running, while liveness and correct decryption add a separate keyper and validator coordination layer.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["gnosis-shutter"]}],"counterfactual":{"summary":"Remaining a small authority-operated xDai chain would have been simpler and potentially easier to coordinate, but would preserve a clear centralization ceiling. Becoming an Ethereum rollup could inherit stronger settlement and bridge conventions, but would trade sovereign validator participation for sequencer and rollup dependencies. Removing bridge pause powers might improve credible-neutrality optics while limiting containment during application incidents. The available evidence supports these trade-offs but does not prove which architecture would have produced more payments, TVL, or revenue.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["gnosis-merge","gnosis-merge-independent","gnosis-bridge","gnosis-bridge-decisions","gnosis-pay-incident","gnosis-tvl"]},"watch":[{"signal":"TVL, multi-currency stablecoin supply, DEX volume, fees, and retained revenue.","implication":"Broad growth would show the payments niche deepening into a larger economy; volume without revenue would keep value capture limited.","source_refs":["gnosis-tvl","gnosis-stables","gnosis-volume","gnosis-fees","gnosis-revenue"]},{"signal":"Bridge-validator composition, light-client adoption, pause decisions, and recovery times.","implication":"More independently verified paths would reduce trusted-bridge exposure; repeated emergency pauses would show control remains a central safety mechanism.","source_refs":["gnosis-bridge","gnosis-bridge-decisions","gnosis-pay-incident"]},{"signal":"Encrypted-mempool participation, keyper diversity, failed decryptions, and fallback behavior.","implication":"Reliable adoption would support Gnosis as a credible-neutrality test bed; thin use or liveness failures would make Shutter an optional niche feature.","source_refs":["gnosis-shutter"]}],"unknowns":[{"question":"What share of current Gnosis activity comes from payments versus trading, incentives, bots, or internal treasury flows?","resolution_trigger":"An independent application- and entity-level fee decomposition."},{"question":"How concentrated are GNO stake, validator operators, and client implementations?","resolution_trigger":"A current validator, entity, and client-diversity audit."},{"question":"What value is exposed to each bridge-validator path and emergency governor set?","resolution_trigger":"A current bridge-by-bridge value and signer map."},{"question":"How many transactions use the encrypted mempool and how often does it fall back to public submission?","resolution_trigger":"Public longitudinal Shutter usage and liveness telemetry."}],"review":{"status":"current","last_reviewed_at":"2026-08-03","next_review_at":"2026-08-10","reviewer":"chaindump-research-desk"}}}')
